# ISO READ BINARY on a 3-octet standard data file with free read access,
# against an EV2. The cases are the five (P1P2, Le) pairs of the unit test
# /ev1-read-binary-reports-short-eof, in order: a read longer than the file, one
# that starts inside it and runs past its end, one that starts at the end of the
# file, one that ends exactly at the end, and Le 0.
# An EV1 reports a read that runs past the end as 6282 with the octets it has.
# An EV3 refuses a read that starts at the very end with 6985 and an empty body
# (measured on a genuine EV3). EV2 behaves like EV1 for the octets but never reports 6282.
#
# Converted from tests/test_dfc_iso_file_access.c test /ev1-read-binary-reports-short-eof (now removed).
# The unit test poked the file and the current-file selection into the engine;
# here the file is created and selected over the wire, with the same octet
# count, ISO file ID 0x1001 and free access rights.
name: vecB ISO READ BINARY end of file on EV2
case-id: vecb-iso-read-binary-short-eof-ev2
origin: synthetic
source: tests/test_dfc_iso_file_access.c#/ev1-read-binary-reports-short-eof
uid: 04112233445566
picc-generation: EV2
picc-storage: 4096

